import Mathlib

/-!
# Bourbaki, rédaction n° 596, §§ 7, 9 and 12: algebras, crossed products, induced modules

Rédaction 596 of the Bourbaki archive (Archives Henri Poincaré, item 1142) is a draft of *Algèbre*,
ch. VIII. This file checks six further places of it. Four are statements false as typed (§ 9
Remarque 3, § 12 Prop. 6 (b), the pencil gloss on § 7 Cor. 4, and § 12 Prop. 26 Cor. 1 for an
imperfect field); two are slips inside proofs whose statement stays true (§ 9 Prop. 12 a),
§ 12 Prop. 3). The statements of §§ 7 and 12 checked earlier are in
`Redaction596Characters.lean`.

**§ 9 n° 4, Remarque 3, p. 147 (false as typed).** Over a locally compact valued field, every
central simple algebra would be a cyclic Galois crossed product `A[E, L]`. Such an algebra has
dimension `[L : K]²` and contains the field `L`. Over `ℂ`, which is locally compact, `M₂(ℂ)` would
need a field extension `L` of `ℂ` of degree `2`, and there is none. The preceding Remarque 2
already names algebraically closed fields as an exception; the remark should require the field to
be non-archimedean (`ℝ` fails too: `M₃(ℝ)` would need a cubic extension).

* `finrank_ne_two`: over an algebraically closed field `k`, no field `L` with `[L : k] = 2`;
* `remark3_fails`: `ℂ` is locally compact and has no extension field of degree `2`.

**§ 9 n° 9, proof of Prop. 12 a), p. 160 (slip in a proof).** In characteristic `p`, `A[a, b)` is
generated by `x`, `y` with `xᵖ - x = a`, `yᵖ = b`, `yx = (x + 1)y`; similarly `u`, `v` for
`A[a', b)`. The proof puts `u₁ = 1 ⊗ u`, `v₁ = y ⊗ v⁻¹` and asserts `v₁u₁ = (u₁ + 1)v₁`. In fact
`v⁻¹u = (u - 1)v⁻¹`, so `v₁u₁ = (u₁ - 1)v₁`. The choice `v₁ = y⁻¹ ⊗ v` gives the stated relation
and still commutes with `x₁ = x ⊗ 1 + 1 ⊗ u`, so Prop. 12 a) stands.

* `inv_mul_eq_sub_one_mul`: if `vu = (u + 1)v` and `w = v⁻¹`, then `wu = (u - 1)w`;
* `typed_v1_mul_u1`: the typed `v₁` satisfies `v₁u₁ = (u₁ - 1)v₁`, in any `A ⊗_K B`;
* `corrected_v1_mul_u1`: `y⁻¹ ⊗ v` satisfies `v₁u₁ = (u₁ + 1)v₁` and commutes with `x₁`;
* `xm`, `ym`, `kr`, `presentation`: a model of `A[0, 1) ≅ M₃(𝔽₃)` by `3 × 3` matrices;
* `prop12a_typed_fails`, `prop12a_corrected`: the same facts checked on `9 × 9` Kronecker
  products over `𝔽₃` by `decide`.

**§ 12 n° 2, proof of Prop. 3, p. 257 (slip in a proof).** The proof says that `ψᵖ χ_E` is an
integral polynomial in the `χ_{Λ^q E}` for `0 ≤ q ≤ p - 1`. Newton's formula (27) needs
`q ≤ p`: already `ψ² χ = χ² - 2 χ_{Λ² E}`. For `G = ℤ/2 = {1, s}`, the permutation
representation on `ℚ²` and the zero representation have the same values at `s` of
`χ_{Λ⁰ E} = 1` and of `χ_E` (namely `1` and `0`), but `(ψ² χ_E)(s) = χ_E(1)` is `2` for one and `0`
for the other. No function at all, polynomial or not, of these values gives `ψ²`. The
proposition holds by (27) with `q ≤ p`.

* `s`, `eq_one_or_eq_s`, `swapMat`, `permHom`, `rhoPerm`, `rhoZero`: the two representations;
* `character_values`: `χ(s) = 0` for both, `χ(s²) = 2` and `0`;
* `prop3_fails`: no `P` with `ψ² χ_E (s) = P (χ_{Λ⁰ E}(s), χ_E(s))` for both.

**§ 12 n° 3, Prop. 6 (b), p. 261 (false as typed).** For a subgroup `H` of `G` and an
`H`-module `F`, `Ind(F)` would be a free `k`-module if and only if `F` is. By (40), `Ind(F)` is,
as a `k`-module, the direct sum of `[G : H]` copies of `F`, and a direct sum of copies of a
non-free projective module can be free. Take `k = ℤ[√-5]`, `H = 1`, `G = ℤ/2`, and `F = I` the
ideal `(2, 1 + √-5)`: then `Ind(F) ≅ I ⊕ I ≅ k²` is free, while `I` is not principal, hence not
free. Assertion (a), for projective modules, is right.

* `β`, `β'`, `I`, `parity`, `one_notMem_I`, `two_dvd_mul`: the ideal and `I · I ⊆ (2)`;
* `not_isPrincipal_I`: `I` is not principal (norms divide `gcd(4, 6) = 2`);
* `T`, `T_bijective`: `(s, t) ↦ (β' s - 2t, βt - 2s)` is an isomorphism `k² ≅ I × I`;
* `free_I_prod_I`, `not_free_I`: `I × I` is free and `I` is not.

**§ 7 n° 3, Cor. 4, pencil gloss, p. 104 (false as written).** For simple `S₀`, `S₁`, the typed
corollary says `S = S₀ ⊗ S₁` is simple if and only if `D = D₀ ⊗ D₁` is a division ring; a pencil
hand glosses the last case as `Z` being a field, `Z = Z₀ ⊗ Z₁` the centre of `D`. For `K = ℝ` and
`A₀ = A₁ = S₀ = S₁ = ℍ`, `Z = ℝ ⊗ ℝ = ℝ` is a field, but `ℍ ⊗_ℝ ℍ` has zero divisors and is
not simple over itself. The typed statement is right.

* `qi`, `qi_mul_qi`, `coord`: the quaternion `i` and a linear form on `ℍ ⊗ ℍ`;
* `zero_divisors`: `(i ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ i)(i ⊗ 1 + 1 ⊗ i) = 0` with both factors nonzero;
* `not_isSimpleModule_quaternion_tensor`: `ℍ ⊗_ℝ ℍ` is not a simple module over itself.

**§ 12 n° 11, Cor. 1 of Prop. 26, p. 286 (false as typed for imperfect `k`).** With
`Γ = Gal(k̄/k)` for an algebraic closure `k̄`, the corollary identifies the `Γ`-invariants of
`k̄ ⊗ R` with `k ⊗ R`, which needs the fixed field of `Γ` to be `k`. For imperfect `k` it is the
perfect closure; a separable closure should be used.

* `intDegree_pow`, `X_ne_pow`: `t` is not a `p`-th power in `𝔽_p(t)`;
* `fixed_not_mem`: in an algebraic closure of `𝔽_p(t)`, `t^{1/p}` is fixed by every automorphism
  and does not lie in `𝔽_p(t)`.

Not formalised: that the quaternion classes form a subgroup of `Br(K)` (§ 9 n° 10, false in
general by Albert's biquaternion division algebras, which need a long construction); the sign
`Ψ(cl A[E, L]) = [E]⁻¹` in §§ 9 n° 3–5 (it requires the crossed-product formalism, and the
theorems survive since inversion is an automorphism); the proof of § 12 Th. 5 (Brauer characters
are not in Mathlib).
-/

namespace Bourbaki.Redaction596Algebras

open TensorProduct

section Remark3

/-- An algebraically closed field has no extension field of degree `2`. -/
theorem finrank_ne_two (k L : Type*) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [Field L] [Algebra k L] :
    Module.finrank k L ≠ 2 := by
  intro h
  have : FiniteDimensional k L := Module.finite_of_finrank_pos (by omega)
  have e : k ≃ₗ[k] L := LinearEquiv.ofBijective (Algebra.linearMap k L)
    (IsAlgClosed.algebraMap_bijective_of_isIntegral (k := k) (K := L))
  have := e.finrank_eq
  rw [Module.finrank_self] at this
  omega

/-- **Remarque 3 fails** for `ℂ`: it is locally compact, and `M₂(ℂ)` is not a crossed product,
since there is no field `L ⊇ ℂ` with `[L : ℂ] = 2`. -/
theorem remark3_fails :
    LocallyCompactSpace ℂ ∧
      ∀ (L : Type) [Field L] [Algebra ℂ L], Module.finrank ℂ L ≠ 2 :=
  ⟨inferInstance, fun L _ _ => finrank_ne_two ℂ L⟩

end Remark3

section Prop12

variable {K A B : Type*} [CommRing K] [Ring A] [Ring B] [Algebra K A] [Algebra K B]

/-- If `vu = (u + 1)v` and `w` is the inverse of `v`, then `wu = (u - 1)w`. -/
theorem inv_mul_eq_sub_one_mul {u v w : B} (hwv : w * v = 1) (hvw : v * w = 1)
    (h : v * u = (u + 1) * v) : w * u = (u - 1) * w := by
  have h1 : u * w = w * (u + 1) := by
    calc u * w = w * (v * u) * w := by rw [← mul_assoc, hwv, one_mul]
    _ = w * ((u + 1) * v) * w := by rw [h]
    _ = w * (u + 1) := by rw [mul_assoc, mul_assoc, hvw, mul_one]
  rw [sub_mul, h1, mul_add, mul_one, one_mul]
  abel

/-- The typed `v₁ = y ⊗ v⁻¹` satisfies `v₁u₁ = (u₁ - 1)v₁`, not `(u₁ + 1)v₁`. -/
theorem typed_v1_mul_u1 (y : A) {u v w : B} (hwv : w * v = 1) (hvw : v * w = 1)
    (h : v * u = (u + 1) * v) :
    (y ⊗ₜ[K] w) * ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[K] u) = ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[K] u - 1) * (y ⊗ₜ[K] w) := by
  rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, mul_one, inv_mul_eq_sub_one_mul hwv hvw h]
  simp only [sub_mul, one_mul, tmul_sub, Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul]

/-- The corrected `v₁ = y⁻¹ ⊗ v` satisfies `v₁u₁ = (u₁ + 1)v₁` and commutes with
`x₁ = x ⊗ 1 + 1 ⊗ u`. Here `z` is the inverse of `y`. -/
theorem corrected_v1_mul_u1 {x y z : A} {u v : B} (hzy : z * y = 1) (hyz : y * z = 1)
    (hy : y * x = (x + 1) * y) (hv : v * u = (u + 1) * v) :
    (z ⊗ₜ[K] v) * ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[K] u) = ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[K] u + 1) * (z ⊗ₜ[K] v) ∧
      (z ⊗ₜ[K] v) * (x ⊗ₜ[K] (1 : B) + (1 : A) ⊗ₜ[K] u) =
        (x ⊗ₜ[K] (1 : B) + (1 : A) ⊗ₜ[K] u) * (z ⊗ₜ[K] v) := by
  have hy' := inv_mul_eq_sub_one_mul hzy hyz hy
  constructor
  · rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, mul_one, hv]
    simp only [add_mul, one_mul, tmul_add, Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul]
  · simp only [mul_add, add_mul, Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, mul_one, one_mul, hy', hv,
      sub_mul, sub_tmul, tmul_add]
    abel

/-- `x = diag(0, 1, 2)` over `𝔽₃`. -/
def xm : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) (ZMod 3) := Matrix.diagonal ![0, 1, 2]

/-- `y`, the cyclic shift `e_j ↦ e_{j-1}` over `𝔽₃`. -/
def ym : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) (ZMod 3) := Matrix.of fun i j => if j = i + 1 then 1 else 0

/-- The Kronecker product `M ⊗ N` of `3 × 3` matrices. -/
abbrev kr (M N : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) (ZMod 3)) :
    Matrix (Fin 3 × Fin 3) (Fin 3 × Fin 3) (ZMod 3) :=
  Matrix.kroneckerMap (· * ·) M N

/-- `x`, `y` satisfy the relations of `A[0, 1)` for `p = 3`: `x³ - x = 0`, `y³ = 1`,
`yx = (x + 1)y`; so `y⁻¹ = y²`. -/
theorem presentation : xm ^ 3 - xm = 0 ∧ ym ^ 3 = 1 ∧ ym * xm = (xm + 1) * ym := by decide

/-- With `u = x`, `v = y`, the typed `v₁ = y ⊗ v⁻¹ = y ⊗ y²` gives `v₁u₁ = (u₁ - 1)v₁`, which is
not `(u₁ + 1)v₁`. -/
theorem prop12a_typed_fails :
    kr ym (ym * ym) * kr 1 xm ≠ (kr 1 xm + 1) * kr ym (ym * ym) ∧
      kr ym (ym * ym) * kr 1 xm = (kr 1 xm - 1) * kr ym (ym * ym) := by decide

/-- The corrected `v₁ = y⁻¹ ⊗ v = y² ⊗ y` gives `v₁u₁ = (u₁ + 1)v₁`, commutes with `x₁`, and
`v₁³ = 1`. -/
theorem prop12a_corrected :
    kr (ym * ym) ym * kr 1 xm = (kr 1 xm + 1) * kr (ym * ym) ym ∧
      kr (ym * ym) ym * (kr xm 1 + kr 1 xm) = (kr xm 1 + kr 1 xm) * kr (ym * ym) ym ∧
      kr (ym * ym) ym ^ 3 = 1 := by decide

end Prop12

section Prop3

open Module

/-- The generator `s` of `ℤ/2`, written multiplicatively. -/
def s : Multiplicative (ZMod 2) := Multiplicative.ofAdd 1

theorem eq_one_or_eq_s (g : Multiplicative (ZMod 2)) : g = 1 ∨ g = s := by
  revert g; decide

theorem s_mul_s : s * s = 1 := by decide

theorem s_ne_one : s ≠ 1 := by decide

/-- The permutation matrix of `ℚ²`. -/
def swapMat : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℚ := !![0, 1; 1, 0]

theorem swapMat_mul_self : swapMat * swapMat = 1 := by
  ext i j; fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [swapMat]

/-- `1 ↦ 1`, `s ↦ swapMat`. -/
def permHom : Multiplicative (ZMod 2) →* Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℚ where
  toFun g := if g = 1 then 1 else swapMat
  map_one' := by simp
  map_mul' a b := by
    rcases eq_one_or_eq_s a with rfl | rfl <;> rcases eq_one_or_eq_s b with rfl | rfl <;>
      simp [s_mul_s, s_ne_one, swapMat_mul_self]

/-- The permutation representation of `ℤ/2` on `ℚ²`. -/
def rhoPerm : Representation ℚ (Multiplicative (ZMod 2)) (Fin 2 → ℚ) :=
  (MonoidHom.ofClass (Matrix.toLinAlgEquiv' (R := ℚ) (n := Fin 2))).comp permHom

/-- The zero representation of `ℤ/2`. -/
def rhoZero : Representation ℚ (Multiplicative (ZMod 2)) PUnit :=
  Representation.trivial ℚ _ PUnit

/-- Both characters vanish at `s`; at `s² = 1` they are the dimensions `2` and `0`. -/
theorem character_values :
    rhoPerm.character s = 0 ∧ rhoZero.character s = 0 ∧
      rhoPerm.character (s * s) = 2 ∧ rhoZero.character (s * s) = 0 := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · change LinearMap.trace ℚ _ (Matrix.toLin' (if s = 1 then 1 else swapMat)) = 0
    simp only [s_ne_one, ↓reduceIte, Matrix.trace_toLin'_eq]
    simp [swapMat, Matrix.trace]
  · rw [Representation.character, Subsingleton.elim (rhoZero s) 0, map_zero]
  · rw [s_mul_s, Representation.char_one]; simp
  · rw [s_mul_s, Representation.char_one, Module.finrank_zero_of_subsingleton]; rfl

/-- **The proof of Prop. 3 fails as typed** for `p = 2`: no function `P` (in particular no integral
polynomial) of `χ_{Λ⁰ E}(s) = 1` and `χ_{Λ¹ E}(s) = χ_E(s)` gives `(ψ² χ_E)(s) = χ_E(s²)` for both
representations. -/
theorem prop3_fails (P : ℚ → ℚ → ℚ) :
    ¬ (P 1 (rhoPerm.character s) = rhoPerm.character (s * s) ∧
        P 1 (rhoZero.character s) = rhoZero.character (s * s)) := by
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4⟩ := character_values
  rintro ⟨e1, e2⟩
  rw [h1, h3] at e1
  rw [h2, h4, e1] at e2
  norm_num at e2

end Prop3

section Prop6

/-- `β = 1 + √-5`. -/
def β : ℤ√(-5) := ⟨1, 1⟩

/-- `β' = 1 - √-5`. -/
def β' : ℤ√(-5) := ⟨1, -1⟩

/-- The ideal `I = (2, 1 + √-5)` of `ℤ[√-5]`. -/
def I : Ideal (ℤ√(-5)) := Ideal.span {2, β}

theorem two_mem_I : (2 : ℤ√(-5)) ∈ I := Ideal.subset_span (by simp)

theorem β_mem_I : β ∈ I := Ideal.subset_span (by simp)

theorem β'_mem_I : β' ∈ I := by
  have : β' = 2 - β := by ext <;> rfl
  rw [this]; exact I.sub_mem two_mem_I β_mem_I

theorem β_mul_β' : β * β' = 6 := by ext <;> rfl

/-- The parity map `ℤ[√-5] → 𝔽₂`, `a + b√-5 ↦ a + b`. -/
def parity : ℤ√(-5) →+* ZMod 2 := Zsqrtd.lift ⟨1, by decide⟩

theorem I_le_ker_parity : I ≤ RingHom.ker parity := by
  rw [I, Ideal.span_le]
  rintro _ (rfl | rfl)
  · simp [parity]; decide
  · simp [parity, β]; decide

theorem one_notMem_I : (1 : ℤ√(-5)) ∉ I := fun h => by
  have := I_le_ker_parity h
  simp [RingHom.mem_ker] at this

/-- `I · I ⊆ (2)`. -/
theorem two_dvd_mul {a b : ℤ√(-5)} (ha : a ∈ I) (hb : b ∈ I) : (2 : ℤ√(-5)) ∣ a * b := by
  have hle : I * I ≤ Ideal.span {2} := by
    rw [I, Ideal.span_mul_span, Ideal.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨x, hx, y, hy, rfl⟩
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    rcases hx with rfl | rfl <;> rcases hy with rfl | rfl
    · exact ⟨2, by ext <;> rfl⟩
    · exact ⟨β, by ext <;> rfl⟩
    · exact ⟨β, by ext <;> rfl⟩
    · exact ⟨⟨-2, 1⟩, by ext <;> rfl⟩
  exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton.mp (hle (Ideal.mul_mem_mul ha hb))

theorem cancel_two {x y : ℤ√(-5)} (h : 2 * x = 2 * y) : x = y := by
  have h1 := congrArg Zsqrtd.re h
  have h2 := congrArg Zsqrtd.im h
  simp [Zsqrtd.re_mul, Zsqrtd.im_mul] at h1 h2
  ext <;> omega

/-- `I` is not principal: a generator would have norm dividing `4` and `6`, hence `1` or `2`;
`a² + 5b² = 2` has no solution, and norm `1` would make `I` the unit ideal. -/
theorem not_isPrincipal_I : ¬ I.IsPrincipal := by
  rintro ⟨g, hg⟩
  have hg' : I = Ideal.span {g} := hg
  have h2 := two_mem_I
  have hβ := β_mem_I
  rw [hg', Ideal.mem_span_singleton] at h2 hβ
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := h2
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hβ
  have n2 := congrArg Zsqrtd.norm hc
  have nβ := congrArg Zsqrtd.norm he
  rw [Zsqrtd.norm_mul] at n2 nβ
  have h4 : (4 : ℤ) = g.norm * c.norm := by rw [← n2]; rfl
  have h6 : (6 : ℤ) = g.norm * e.norm := by rw [← nβ]; rfl
  have hd : g.norm ∣ 2 := by
    have := dvd_sub (Dvd.intro _ h6.symm) (Dvd.intro _ h4.symm)
    norm_num at this
    exact this
  have hn0 : 0 ≤ g.norm := Zsqrtd.norm_nonneg (by norm_num) g
  have hle : g.norm ≤ 2 := Int.le_of_dvd (by norm_num) hd
  have hne : g.norm ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0; rw [h0] at hd; norm_num at hd
  have hnd := Zsqrtd.norm_def g
  interval_cases hn : g.norm
  · exact absurd hn0 (by omega)
  · have hu : IsUnit g := (Zsqrtd.norm_eq_one_iff' (by norm_num) g).mp hn
    apply one_notMem_I
    rw [hg', Ideal.span_singleton_eq_top.mpr hu]
    exact Submodule.mem_top
  · have h1 : g.re ≤ 1 := by nlinarith [mul_self_nonneg g.im, mul_self_nonneg g.re]
    have h2 : -1 ≤ g.re := by nlinarith [mul_self_nonneg g.im, mul_self_nonneg g.re]
    have h3 : g.im ≤ 0 := by nlinarith [mul_self_nonneg g.im, mul_self_nonneg g.re]
    have h4 : 0 ≤ g.im := by nlinarith [mul_self_nonneg g.im, mul_self_nonneg g.re]
    interval_cases g.re <;> interval_cases g.im <;> omega

/-- The map `k² → I × I`, `(s, t) ↦ (β' s - 2t, βt - 2s)`, with matrix `T = [[β', -2], [-2, β]]`;
`S = [[β, 2], [2, β']]` satisfies `S T = T S = 2`. -/
def T : (ℤ√(-5) × ℤ√(-5)) →ₗ[ℤ√(-5)] (I × I) :=
  LinearMap.prod
    ((LinearMap.fst _ _ _).smulRight (⟨β', β'_mem_I⟩ : I) -
      (LinearMap.snd _ _ _).smulRight (⟨2, two_mem_I⟩ : I))
    ((LinearMap.snd _ _ _).smulRight (⟨β, β_mem_I⟩ : I) -
      (LinearMap.fst _ _ _).smulRight (⟨2, two_mem_I⟩ : I))

theorem T_apply (p : ℤ√(-5) × ℤ√(-5)) :
    ((T p).1 : ℤ√(-5)) = p.1 * β' - p.2 * 2 ∧ ((T p).2 : ℤ√(-5)) = p.2 * β - p.1 * 2 := by
  simp [T]

/-- `T` is bijective: injective since `S T = 2`, surjective since `S (I × I) ⊆ 2 k²`. -/
theorem T_bijective : Function.Bijective T := by
  constructor
  · intro p q hpq
    obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := T_apply p
    obtain ⟨h3, h4⟩ := T_apply q
    have e1 : ((T p).1 : ℤ√(-5)) = (T q).1 := by rw [hpq]
    have e2 : ((T p).2 : ℤ√(-5)) = (T q).2 := by rw [hpq]
    rw [h1, h3] at e1
    rw [h2, h4] at e2
    have hb := β_mul_β'
    refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_
    · exact cancel_two (by linear_combination β * e1 + 2 * e2 + (q.1 - p.1) * hb)
    · exact cancel_two (by linear_combination 2 * e1 + β' * e2 + (q.2 - p.2) * hb)
  · rintro ⟨a, b⟩
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ : (2 : ℤ√(-5)) ∣ β * a + 2 * b := by
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := two_dvd_mul β_mem_I a.2
      exact ⟨c + b, by rw [hc]; ring⟩
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ : (2 : ℤ√(-5)) ∣ 2 * a + β' * b := by
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := two_dvd_mul β'_mem_I b.2
      exact ⟨a + c, by rw [hc]; ring⟩
    refine ⟨(s, t), ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := T_apply (s, t)
    have hb := β_mul_β'
    refine Prod.ext (Subtype.ext ?_) (Subtype.ext ?_)
    · rw [h1]
      exact cancel_two (by linear_combination -β' * hs + 2 * ht + (a : ℤ√(-5)) * hb)
    · rw [h2]
      exact cancel_two (by linear_combination 2 * hs - β * ht + (b : ℤ√(-5)) * hb)

/-- `I ⊕ I ≅ k²` is free: this is `Ind(I)` for `H = 1 ⊂ G = ℤ/2`, by (40). -/
theorem free_I_prod_I : Module.Free (ℤ√(-5)) (I × I) :=
  Module.Free.of_equiv (LinearEquiv.ofBijective T T_bijective)

/-- **Prop. 6 (b) fails**: `I` is not free, since a free ideal has rank `≤ 1` and is then
principal. -/
theorem not_free_I : ¬ Module.Free (ℤ√(-5)) I := by
  intro _
  apply not_isPrincipal_I
  rw [← Submodule.rank_le_one_iff_isPrincipal]
  exact (Submodule.rank_le I).trans (Module.rank_self (ℤ√(-5))).le

end Prop6

section Cor4Gloss

open Quaternion

/-- The quaternion `i`. -/
def qi : ℍ[ℝ] := ⟨0, 1, 0, 0⟩

theorem qi_mul_qi : qi * qi = -1 := by ext <;> simp [qi]

/-- The linear form `x ⊗ y ↦ x₁ y₀` on `ℍ ⊗_ℝ ℍ` (coefficient of `i` times real part). -/
def coord : ℍ[ℝ] ⊗[ℝ] ℍ[ℝ] →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ :=
  TensorProduct.lift (LinearMap.mk₂ ℝ (fun x y : ℍ[ℝ] => x.imI * y.re)
    (fun _ _ _ => by simp [add_mul]) (fun _ _ _ => by simp [mul_assoc])
    (fun _ _ _ => by simp [mul_add]) (fun _ _ _ => by simp; ring))

theorem coord_tmul (x y : ℍ[ℝ]) : coord (x ⊗ₜ y) = x.imI * y.re := by
  simp [coord]

/-- `(i ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ i)(i ⊗ 1 + 1 ⊗ i) = i² ⊗ 1 - 1 ⊗ i² = 0`, both factors nonzero. -/
theorem zero_divisors :
    (qi ⊗ₜ[ℝ] (1 : ℍ[ℝ]) - 1 ⊗ₜ qi) * (qi ⊗ₜ 1 + 1 ⊗ₜ qi) = 0 ∧
      qi ⊗ₜ[ℝ] (1 : ℍ[ℝ]) - 1 ⊗ₜ qi ≠ 0 ∧ qi ⊗ₜ[ℝ] (1 : ℍ[ℝ]) + 1 ⊗ₜ qi ≠ 0 := by
  refine ⟨?_, fun h => ?_, fun h => ?_⟩
  · simp only [sub_mul, mul_add, Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, one_mul, mul_one,
      qi_mul_qi, TensorProduct.neg_tmul, TensorProduct.tmul_neg]
    abel
  · have := congrArg coord h
    simp [coord_tmul, qi] at this
  · have := congrArg coord h
    simp [coord_tmul, qi] at this

/-- **The pencil gloss fails**: `Z = ℝ ⊗ ℝ` is a field, yet `S = ℍ ⊗_ℝ ℍ` is not a simple module
over `B = ℍ ⊗_ℝ ℍ`. -/
theorem not_isSimpleModule_quaternion_tensor :
    ¬ IsSimpleModule (ℍ[ℝ] ⊗[ℝ] ℍ[ℝ]) (ℍ[ℝ] ⊗[ℝ] ℍ[ℝ]) := by
  rw [isSimpleModule_self_iff_isUnit]
  rintro ⟨-, h⟩
  obtain ⟨h0, h1, h2⟩ := zero_divisors
  exact h2 ((h _ h1).mul_right_eq_zero.mp h0)

end Cor4Gloss

section Prop26

variable (p : ℕ) [hp : Fact p.Prime]

theorem intDegree_pow {K : Type*} [Field K] {y : RatFunc K} (hy : y ≠ 0) (n : ℕ) :
    (y ^ n).intDegree = n * y.intDegree := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [pow_succ, RatFunc.intDegree_mul (pow_ne_zero n hy) hy, ih]
    push_cast; ring

/-- `t` is not a `p`-th power in `𝔽_p(t)`: its degree `1` is not divisible by `p`. -/
theorem X_ne_pow (y : RatFunc (ZMod p)) : y ^ p ≠ RatFunc.X := by
  intro h
  have hy : y ≠ 0 := by
    rintro rfl
    rw [zero_pow hp.out.ne_zero] at h
    exact RatFunc.X_ne_zero h.symm
  have := congrArg RatFunc.intDegree h
  rw [intDegree_pow hy, RatFunc.intDegree_X] at this
  have hd : ((p : ℕ) : ℤ) ∣ ((1 : ℕ) : ℤ) := ⟨_, by simpa using this.symm⟩
  have := Nat.le_of_dvd one_pos (Int.natCast_dvd_natCast.mp hd)
  exact absurd hp.out.one_lt (by omega)

/-- **The fixed field of `Aut(k̄/k)` is not `k`** for `k = 𝔽_p(t)`: a `p`-th root of `t` is fixed
by every `k`-automorphism (Frobenius is injective) but is not in `k`. -/
theorem fixed_not_mem : ∃ x : AlgebraicClosure (RatFunc (ZMod p)),
    (∀ σ : AlgebraicClosure (RatFunc (ZMod p)) ≃ₐ[RatFunc (ZMod p)]
      AlgebraicClosure (RatFunc (ZMod p)), σ x = x) ∧
    x ∉ Set.range (algebraMap (RatFunc (ZMod p)) (AlgebraicClosure (RatFunc (ZMod p)))) := by
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := IsAlgClosed.exists_pow_nat_eq
    (algebraMap (RatFunc (ZMod p)) (AlgebraicClosure (RatFunc (ZMod p))) RatFunc.X)
    hp.out.pos
  refine ⟨x, fun σ => ?_, ?_⟩
  · apply frobenius_inj (AlgebraicClosure (RatFunc (ZMod p))) p
    simp only [frobenius_def]
    rw [← map_pow, hx, AlgEquiv.commutes]
  · rintro ⟨y, rfl⟩
    rw [← map_pow] at hx
    exact X_ne_pow p y ((algebraMap _ _).injective hx)

end Prop26

